  m_Name: unit_730165
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  unitName: Knight Perceval (EU)
  unitId: 730165
  unitNumber: 7116
  description: "As Perceval was travelling along the road, every few weeks he managed
    to spot clay shards of various sizes between the rubble on the ground. The loyal
    knight still had no idea why he was collecting them, but he kept going anyway.
    The longer Perceval travelled, the more assaults from evil forces he faced. No
    matter where he went, the dark creatures never allowed him to get some rest.
    There were moments when he thought he was done for, but surprising even himself,
    eventually the most terrifying of his assailants were no match for him any longer.
    Using the photon blade bestowed upon him by King Arthur, he was able to conjure
    powerful tremors and gusts to defeat his foes. That would not be his only surprise.
    When he stopped walking to admire nature, which he enjoyed doing occasionally,
    it seemed like the flowers bloomed before his eyes. \u201CIs this really happening,
    or are my weary eyes deceiving me?\u201D he said with a wondering voice. After
    many long years passing like an endless nightmare, Perceval heard about several
    fellow Knights of the Round Table who died during their quest. Thinking he was
    the only one left, he wished to return to King Arthur\u2026 but at this moment,
    it would mean coming back empty handed. Perceval's total dedication to his quest
    meant he would not allow himself to fail his king and best friend. One night,
    he had an unusual dream. It was clouded, and through the fog he saw the visage
    of what looked like an old man. It suddenly started speaking, but out of the
    old man's mouth came out a dark demonic voice. It told Perceval that he had finally
    completed his quest. All along, the weary knight had been collecting shards which
    were fragments of the Holy Grail itself! As the dream went on, Perceval learned
    of an ancient sacred ritual which, according to the demonic voice, could reforge
    the Grail into the relic of power it was supposed to be!"
  summonDesc: My sword and I vow to complete this grand quest for you... My King!
  fusionDesc: Where is this leading me? I must not fail in my quest!
  evoDesc: My sword and I vow to complete this grand quest for you... My King!
